  "description": "Fuaran.Core.Lease — a generic lease/claim strand: claims over an abstract resource axis (Claim / Release / Expire) with a total apply / canApply where a conflicting claim is a typed rejection enumerating the current holder and the overlapping resources, a canonical wire codec, and a Fuaran.Core.OpStream StreamWitness — so lease history is an append-only, hash-chained, replayable, tamper-evident stream. The resource axis reuses Fuaran.Core.Tree's IdWitness (no new witness shape); expiry takes time as data (the host supplies \"now\"; Core reads no clock), so replay is deterministic. Generalises the coordination a multi-agent dispatcher hand-rolls. FSharp.Core only, Fable-clean.",
